>
> Because i know how y'all react to the subject of various created 
> orthographies, etc. etc. etc. and everybody basically agrees that the 
> standard orthography should officially be this one, i have a different 
> question. What orthography do you use to write lojban, and why? 


I use the Latin alphabet as described in the grammar book. This includes 
using capital letters for stress in cmene. Sometimes, I practice using 
Elian script but the letters tend to be too large.

